If you keep your books in a spreadsheet, you can carry on under Making Tax Digital for VAT. You need bridging software to send the return, and DIY Accounting Submit™ is bridging software.

Type your final figures into the nine boxes, or drop a DIY Accounting spreadsheet or a DIYA-GL™ book on the page to fill them in. Check them, then send. HMRC's receipt comes straight back.

99p a month. Start with {offer}: {link}

You can send a real VAT return to HMRC with DIY Accounting Submit™ without paying. Start with {offer}.

Sign in with your Google account, then connect to HMRC with your Government Gateway details. Pick the VAT period that is due, fill in the nine boxes and send. You get HMRC's receipt with its Form Bundle Number.

If you want to keep going, it is 99p a month. {link}

Making Tax Digital for VAT covers every VAT-registered business, whatever its turnover. Your first VAT period that started on or after 1 April 2022 was the first one under the rule.

It means your VAT return goes to HMRC from software. DIY Accounting Submit™ is HMRC recognised software for it, and it is listed on HMRC's software finder.

99p a month. Start with {offer}: {link}

A VAT return is done when HMRC says so. With DIY Accounting Submit™ you see HMRC's answer on the page: the receipt with its Form Bundle Number, your proof that you sent it.

You can also see which VAT periods are open and which are done, and look up any return you have sent before, straight from HMRC.

99p a month. Start with {offer}: {link}

DIY Accounting Submit™ is our Making Tax Digital software, from the family company behind DIY Accounting Spreadsheets™.

It sends your VAT return to HMRC from the figures you already keep: type them into the nine boxes, or drop your DIY Accounting spreadsheet on the page. HMRC's receipt comes back with its Form Bundle Number.

99p a month, cancel any time. Start with {offer}: {link}

Our Basic Sole Trader package is the simplest set of DIY Accounting Spreadsheets™. It is for sole traders who are not VAT registered and have no employees.

You get a sales spreadsheet and a purchases spreadsheet. The accounts add them up into a profit and loss account and the figures for the short self-employed tax return.

It works in Microsoft Excel and OpenOffice Calc, comes with a step-by-step guide, and is free to download: {link}

Our Self Employed package of DIY Accounting Spreadsheets™ is for anyone self-employed, whether VAT registered or not, with or without employees.

It covers sales and purchases, cash and bank reconciliation, VAT returns, and the profit and loss account. It produces the figures for both the short and the full self-employed tax return.

It works in Microsoft Excel and OpenOffice Calc, and it is free to download: {link}

Our Company Accounts package of DIY Accounting Spreadsheets™ is for limited companies, VAT registered or not, with or without employees.

It uses double-entry bookkeeping and works with our payroll spreadsheets. It produces VAT returns, the profit and loss account, the balance sheet, year-end accounts for Companies House, and the CT600 Corporation Tax figures.

It works in Microsoft Excel and OpenOffice Calc, and it is free to download: {link}

Our Taxi Driver package of DIY Accounting Spreadsheets™ is made for taxi and private hire work.

It has the income and expense headings a driver needs, and it produces the figures for your self assessment tax return.

It works in Microsoft Excel and OpenOffice Calc, and it is free to download: {link}

DIY Accounting Spreadsheets™ are Excel workbooks for UK small business bookkeeping and accounts, designed by a Chartered Management Accountant.

There is a package for sole traders, the self-employed, limited companies and taxi drivers, and one for payslips. Each covers sales, purchases, profit and loss and the tax figures for that kind of business.

They work in Microsoft Excel and OpenOffice Calc, come with step-by-step guides, and are free to download: {link}

